<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirpur Khas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirpur Khas is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>. Founded in 1806 by Mir Ali Murad Talpur, it was the seat of a branch of the Talpur dynasty until the British conquest of 1843. It is now a market centre for a farming region known for its mangoes, and the remains of an ancient Buddhist stupa stand nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirpur-khas.jpg" alt="Mirpur Khas" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saqib Qayyum · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomb_of_Mir_Tharo_Talpur_%E2%80%94_the_ruler_of_Mirpur_Khas_%E2%80%94_in_Chitorri_Graveyard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
